### 1. Get a CSRF token; the HTTP client keeps the session cookie.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {%
    client.global.set("csrfToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 2. Wrong password — expect 401 (use an existing account).
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "nazar.registration.check01@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 3. Unknown email — expect the same 401 message.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "unknown.login.check@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 4. Valid credentials — expect 204 and a rotated session cookie.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "nazar.registration.check01@example.com",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}

### 5. Refresh the CSRF token after successful login.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {%
    client.global.set("csrfToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 6. Missing CSRF token — expect 403.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nazar.registration.check01@example.com",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}
